  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The mid-point of a line segment joining the points&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Given, the centroid&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>G</mi></math> is the mid-point of the&nbsp;line segment joining the points&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>,&nbsp;thus&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>G</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>Also, given circumcentre&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> is origin&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>We know that, for a triangle circumcentre, orthocentre and centroid are collinear.</p><p>Thus,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>G</mi></math>&nbsp;and orthocentre <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>H</mi></math> are collinear.</p><p>Again, we know that the equation of a line passing through the points&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Thus, the orthocentre lies&nbsp;on the line joining the points&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and its equation, is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></mfrac><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p>",
